# The dealing pass, in a process of its own.
#
# **This exists because dealing used to sit behind the analysis.** The
# scheduler daemon runs its jobs sequentially -- ingest, then the pipeline,
# then dealing -- so the lightest, most time-critical job in the system was
# queued behind the heaviest. On 2026-09-11 the pipeline wedged at 13:35 and
# the account was not dealt for again that session: not one open, and far
# worse not one CLOSE. A position that needed flattening at the bell was
# waiting on a three-and-a-half-year backtest to finish.
#
# Separating them means a slow, stuck or failed analysis can no longer strand
# the book. The worst it can now do is leave the dealer acting on an ageing
# view, and that is guarded rather than hoped about: `decision_is_stale`
# withholds OPENS on a decision bar older than two bar spacings, and never
# blocks a close.
#
# Nothing here computes a rule. It reads the target units the engine already
# persisted -- `persist.intent` remains the single owner of what should be
# held -- and turns them into orders. That is what keeps this inside the "one
# engine, and it is the production one" constraint: that rule is about who
# DECIDES a position, and this process decides none.
#
# It does not conflict with cfdinvest.service. It must not: the whole point
# is that it keeps running when the daemon is busy. `trade-capital` has been
# removed from the daemon's job list so the two cannot both deal.

[Unit]
Description=cfdinvest dealing pass (Capital demo account)
After=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=cfdinvest
Group=cfdinvest
WorkingDirectory=/opt/cfdinvest
EnvironmentFile=/etc/cfdinvest/env

ExecStart=/opt/cfdinvest/.venv/bin/cfdinvest-schedule trade-capital

# Light by construction: it reads one row of a persisted run, asks the broker
# what it holds, and places orders. If it ever needs a gigabyte, something has
# been added to it that does not belong -- the ceiling is here to say so
# loudly rather than to throttle it quietly. MemoryMax kills; MemoryHigh
# would sleep it on every allocation and hide the problem, which is the exact
# failure that cost 2026-09-09 and 2026-09-11.
MemoryMax=1G

# A pass must never outlive its own cadence. Stuck is a state this whole unit
# exists to make survivable, so it is bounded rather than trusted.
TimeoutStartSec=240

ProtectSystem=strict
ProtectHome=true
PrivateTmp=true
NoNewPrivileges=true
RestrictAddressFamilies=AF_INET AF_INET6 AF_UNIX
ReadOnlyPaths=/opt/cfdinvest
ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/cfdinvest

StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal
SyslogIdentifier=cfdinvest-dealer
